+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Greenfield bootstrap state
+- No `RIGGING.md` and no production code yet (`index.html`, `js/app.js`, `css/app.css` absent). This is a greenfield build per the Shipshape routing: stay on deck, author specs and watchbill, then stop.
+- The harness is already present: `package.json` and `node_modules` provide `@cucumber/cucumber` and `happy-dom`. `README.md` states `features/support/world.js` loads the real `index.html` + `js/app.js` into a happy-dom window before each scenario.
+- Before QM can run the watchbill, Shipwright must fit out `RIGGING.md` (language, directories, methods, perturbation, tiers) and `AGENTS.md`. Captain does not write those files.
+
+## Decisions carried into the build
+- Stack: vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors. DOM-level Cucumber scenarios live in `features/`; step definitions belong in `features/support/`.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanilla` (framework slug = "vanilla"), storing `{id, title, completed}` items. Editing state is not persisted.
+- Base markup: `assets/app-template.index.html` becomes `index.html`; strip comments and update relative asset paths. New-todo input keeps the `autofocus` attribute.
+
+## Open questions for the user
+- Confirm the framework slug for the localStorage key (`todos-vanilla` assumed).
+- Confirm whether `todomvc-common` / `todomvc-app-css` (referenced by the template's `<link>` tags) should be vendored as real dependencies or replaced by a local `css/app.css`.
diff --git a/features/todo-counter.feature b/features/todo-counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..86b3d79
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter and clearing completed
+  As a user of the todo list
+  I want to see how many todos remain active
+  So that I can gauge my remaining work
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows 0 items left when empty
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then the todo count reads "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows 1 item left for one active todo
+    Given the todo list has todos "A"
+    Then the todo count reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows 2 items left for two active todos
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    Then the todo count reads "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter counts only active todos
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    And the user checks the todo "A"
+    Then the todo count reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: The clear-completed button is hidden when nothing is completed
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: The clear-completed button removes completed todos
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    And the user checks the todo "A"
+    When the user clicks "Clear completed"
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "B"
+    And the clear-completed button is hidden
diff --git a/features/todo-creation.feature b/features/todo-creation.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..72d8b71
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-creation.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: Todo creation
+  As a user of the todo list
+  I want to add new todos
+  So that I can track the work I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: A new todo is added on Enter
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only input is ignored
+    When the user types "   " into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed from the title
+    When the user types "  Walk the dog  " into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: The new-todo input is focused on load
+    Then the new-todo input is focused
+
+  Scenario: The main and footer sections are hidden when there are no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: The main and footer sections are shown once a todo exists
+    When the user adds a todo titled "First"
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..87d6e64
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user of the todo list
+  I want to edit a todo's title
+  So that I can correct mistakes
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters editing mode
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on Enter and exits editing mode
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy soy milk" into the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "Buy soy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy soy milk" does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on blur and exits editing mode
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy oat milk" into the edit input and blurs the field
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards the edit
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy almond milk" into the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Editing trims the saved title
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "  Buy rice milk  " into the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "Buy rice milk"
+
+  Scenario: The destroy button removes a todo
+    Given the todo list has todos "Buy milk" and "B"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "B"
diff --git a/features/todo-routing.feature b/features/todo-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c92a078
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+Feature: Persistence and routing
+  As a user of the todo list
+  I want my todos and active filter to persist
+  So that I can return to my list later
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist to localStorage across reload
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    When the todo list is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows two todos titled "A" and "B"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists across reload
+    Given the todo list has todos "A"
+    And the user checks the todo "A"
+    When the todo list is reloaded
+    Then the todo "A" has the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the todo list has todos "A"
+    And the todo "A" is in editing mode
+    When the todo list is reloaded
+    Then the todo "A" does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists across reload
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    And the user checks the todo "A"
+    When the user opens the "Completed" filter
+    And the todo list is reloaded
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+    And the todo list shows one todo with the title "A"
+
+  Scenario: The active filter hides non-matching todos
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    And the user checks the todo "A"
+    When the user opens the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "B"
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it under the Active filter
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    And the user opens the "Active" filter
+    When the user checks the todo "A"
+    Then the todo list shows one todo with the title "B"
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows all todos
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+    And the user opens the "Completed" filter
+    When the user opens the "All" filter
+    Then the todo list shows two todos titled "A" and "B"
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
diff --git a/features/todo-toggling.feature b/features/todo-toggling.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..36f0f59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-toggling.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Todo completion toggling
+  As a user of the todo list
+  I want to mark todos complete or active
+  So that I can track what is done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo list has todos "A" and "B"
+
+  Scenario: Checking a single todo marks it completed
+    When the user checks the todo "A"
+    Then the todo "A" has the class "completed"
+    And the todo "B" does not have the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox is unchecked until all todos complete
+    When the user checks the todo "A"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox reflects full completion
+    When the user checks the todo "A"
+    And the user checks the todo "B"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+    And the todo "A" has the class "completed"
+    And the todo "B" has the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles every todo
+    When the user checks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "A" has the class "completed"
+    And the todo "B" has the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete is cleared after clear-completed
+    And the user checks the toggle-all checkbox
+    When the user clicks "Clear completed"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
